Spring Boot Microservice Example

    Advantages
            Simplifies complex APIs.
            Reduces coupling between clients and subsystems.
            Improves readability.
            Makes controllers/services thinner.
            Encapsulates orchestration logic in one place.
            Easier to maintain and extend.


    Disadvantages
            A facade can become a "God class" if it accumulates too many responsibilities.
            It may hide subsystem features that some clients actually need.
            It introduces an additional layer of abstraction.

